  "subtitle": "Capture presenting concern, patient goal, referral, and accessibility; confirm clinician review and care handoff.",
  "description": "Therapy Intake records presenting concern, patient goal, referral, accessibility, clinician review, and care handoff. Therapy Intake evidence stays linked.",
  "use_case": "Use this therapy intake time-ordered tracking when staff must document presenting concern and patient goal. Reconcile referral, accessibility, clinician review, and care handoff before the therapy intake handoff. Use the patient narrative, referral documents, accessibility request, urgent-concern routing, clinician questions, modality preference, scheduling handoff, and receipt confirmation. This intake preserves the person's presenting narrative, counseling goals, referral context, communication access, urgent routing, clinician questions, modality preference, and first-session handoff. Keep self-described stressors, strengths, supports, prior service context, language preference, sensory or mobility access, immediate resource needs, screening provenance, and intake disposition visible. Ask the assigned therapy intake reviewer to confirm presenting concern against the organization's policy.",
  "risk_tier": "C",
